{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>קֹדֶשׁ לַה׳.</b> This implies that any form in which ״קֹדֶשׁ לַה׳״ is written is valid. And what the Gemara says there (Shabbat 63b) — that it was written in two lines, yod hei above, ״קֹדֶשׁ לַה׳״ below — was not as a requirement. And so you will find there that Rabbi Eliezer son of Rabbi Yose said: I saw it in Rome, and ״קֹדֶשׁ לַה׳״ was written on it in a single line, etc. — see, then, that the matter is not a requirement, and even according to the first Tanna it is not a requirement. With this it will not be difficult in your eyes, the ruling of the Rambam (Hilkhot Kelei HaMikdash chapter 9) — one should examine there."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:12.645595383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}